{"id": "EUVD-2026-68916", "enisaUuid": "93c6c6c1-d897-36fa-acd6-120869f75515", "description": "A vulnerability in the Backblaze Client allows a local user to make the system not bootable by creating a link from Backblaze's folder to Windows OS system files during a backup. Successful exploitation requires an administrator-level system change that results in the absence of specific Windows OS security controls. This vulnerability is due to improper link resolution.", "datePublished": "2026-09-01T00:13:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-10T23:32:25", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:H/SI:L/SA:L", "references": ["https://www.backblaze.com/computer-backup/docs/backup-client-release-notes-windows", "https://www.backblaze.com/status/update"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-19820", "GHSA-wf7j-r93f-5cvm"], "assigner": "Bugcrowd", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "53323e8e-4ef8-3465-9a0d-9f8d3597cb0f", "product": {"name": "Backblaze Client", "vendor": {"name": "Backblaze"}}, "product_version": "10.0.1.1037"}, {"id": "ca83ee3c-0c5d-3dea-a3eb-2ae801ead355", "product": {"name": "Backblaze Client", "vendor": {"name": "Backblaze"}}, "product_version": "10.0.2.1047"}, {"id": "d03785f9-bd49-3410-bb48-dbc9bc67467c", "product": {"name": "Backblaze Client", "vendor": {"name": "Backblaze"}}, "product_version": "10.0.0.1029"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8cc6fe0a-6bf4-3450-b9ab-1c6760a9d843", "vendor": {"name": "Backblaze"}}], "isExploited": false}